ere, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $2(k+3t)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3t}{2(k+3t)}+\\frac{k}{k+3t} & = \\\\ \\frac{3t}{2(k+3t)}+\\frac{2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{k}{k+3t} & = \\\\ \\frac{3t}{2(k+3t)}+\\frac{2k}{2(k+3t)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3t+2k}{2(k+3t)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb2231aa-8afa-57df-a43c-cb3add25b2cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection/4e56664466b0468c952be9020af7fa52779032be21ed592e49d05c05d8e2b1ac" :answer/id #uuid "40a6b1b0-cd27-556b-a616-c849f8373410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3n-2}{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection/e7179e48b274571a49f00912ded627f8daa18d75bdb4a47b4ff5bddbb4f4692b" :answer/id #uuid "eafb2417-5183-5106-b91c-d554a54996e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5n+4}{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection/b3214d595aeef2eb4e2ba9e363dd92f1663909ab1811f98b6e3957f0c5cb7741" :answer/id #uuid "71fd9806-50ac-5cdf-a503-dd74cd0b14e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7n-4}{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection/d35139435093138595ab80b1123732698b129e1b42df219d5c343aa5453491cd" :answer/id #uuid "b2c73fa1-e9fd-565e-b9c9-8acca44b6459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3n+2}{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection/19b2e09f317e50d32f4f5b9ad5562d82ca17a7fb0bdfe35e8ef9f818a0f4d8c6" :answer/id #uuid "5f4454ad-7f7a-51aa-b749-67d749dafbd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7n+2}{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c1cca89-ea8c-53d4-88b6-17a5f1c0ba3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113291/selection/19b2e09f317e50d32f4f5b9ad5562d82ca17a7fb0bdfe35e8ef9f818a0f4d8c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-113291/selection/4e56664466b0468c952be9020af7fa52779032be21ed592e49d05c05d8e2b1ac" "q-113291/selection/e7179e48b274571a49f00912ded627f8daa18d75bdb4a47b4ff5bddbb4f4692b" "q-113291/selection/b3214d595aeef2eb4e2ba9e363dd92f1663909ab1811f98b6e3957f0c5cb7741" "q-113291/selection/d35139435093138595ab80b1123732698b129e1b42df219d5c343aa5453491cd" "q-113291/selection/19b2e09f317e50d32f4f5b9ad5562d82ca17a7fb0bdfe35e8ef9f818a0f4d8c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113291" :question/id #uuid "c78ad5bb-bc8b-5f94-a2c4-c8f19012e47a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113291" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}=b$ and $\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}=c,$ what is $b-c?$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to subtract the following fractions:\n\n$$\nb-c=\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}\n$$\n\nIn order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $n-2$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{(-1)}{(-1)}\\cdot \\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{-2n+1}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(5n+3)-(-2n+1)}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3+2n-1}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{7n+2}{n-2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8058df30-04de-555c-adfa-61fbf2b0ff31"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113315/selection/48ab58e5ddffb008dd95ec96c9b6c43acdb913fcf30431c4c7f9404c85270a9f" :answer/id #uuid "8f14af5e-a475-526b-b312-49c4de7c0b4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5d+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/va